---
import { Footer } from "@/components/footer";
import { Header } from "@/components/header";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Sift"
  description="Privacy policy for the Sift browser extension"
>
  <div class="page">
    <Header />
    <main>
      <div class="content">
        <a href="/" class="back-link">
          &larr; Back to home
        </a>

        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

        <div class="sections">
          <section>
            <h2>What information does this extension collect?</h2>
            <p>
              As a user is browsing movies / shows on an OTT platform's website, this extension scrapes the web page to identify the movies / shows being shown to the user.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>How is this information used?</h2>
            <p>
              Once the movies / shows on the web page have been identified, their IMDB rating and related information is retrieved via a web request to a third-party, and the ratings are displayed to the user next to the movie tile.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>What information does this extension share with third-parties?</h2>
            <div class="section-copy">
              <p>
                The extension sends a movie's title and year of release to <a href="https://www.omdbapi.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">omdbapi.com</a>, which is an API service providing movie ratings from IMDB and similar providers. omdbapi.com sends the IMDB rating (and some related info) back.
              </p>
              <p>
                If the user explicitly opts-in to error reporting, any errors that occur during use of the extension are reported (along with related details like device, OS, browser, browser dimensions, etc.) to our error reporting platform - <a href="https://sentry.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">sentry.io</a>.
              </p>
              <p>A full list of the data collected is shown to the user in the extension's popup, where the user can choose whether or not to opt-in to error reporting.</p>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 100vh; }
  main { flex: 1; }
  .content { width: min(100% - 2rem, 48rem); margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 0; }
  .back-link { display: inline-flex; margin-bottom: 2rem; color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: .875rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--foreground); }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: var(--foreground); font-size: 2.25rem; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .sections { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--foreground); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-foreground); line-height: 1.625; }
  .section-copy { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .section-copy a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .section-copy a:hover { color: var(--foreground); }
</style>
